types.description:
Platform security operations using the latest active merchant key.
Adapters compose canonical text; the platform owns subject construction and key lookup.
Each operation has a dedicated request and does not accept historical key versions.

@author IAIS
@version PlatformChannelSecurityService.java, v 0.1 2026-09-17 IAIS

methods.description:
Select the latest signing key and delegate signature calculation to IBCM.

@param request merchant, signing algorithm and exact canonical text
@return unchanged IBCM signature: HMAC_SHA256 uses lowercase HEX;
        current other enabled algorithms use Base64

Verify the original text using one latest active verification key, without historical fallback.
IBCM may also return false for internal verification failures; false does not uniquely identify a mismatch.
@param request merchant, algorithm, original text and signature in the selected algorithm's native format
@return IBCM verification result; platform validation and key lookup failures throw an exception

Encrypt through IBCM; asymmetric encryption uses the institution public key.
@param request merchant, cipher category, algorithm, payload and algorithm-specific parameters
@return IBCM ciphertext, or armored/Base64 PGP packet; block-cipher IVs are not prepended

Decrypt through IBCM; asymmetric decryption uses the platform private key.
@param request merchant, cipher category, algorithm, ciphertext and matching parameters
@return IBCM result: SM2 and SM2_CITICSH return Base64 plaintext; other algorithms return text

Calculate an unkeyed SHA digest without merchant identification or key lookup.
@param request digest algorithm, original text and output encoding
@return encoded digest; this cannot replace keyed signature verification

Obtain one latest active key for custom in-process calculation, preserving the platform request context.
Missing material throws instead of returning null. Returned version is metadata, not a selector.
Material retains its stored format and must never be logged, persisted by the adapter or sent in a message.
@param request merchant, computation purpose and key classification
@return one key material for local custom calculation

